From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a frame gets the monitor it is on as its screen

A <webview>'s page is a child frame of the desk page, and a child frame
inherits its parent's screens. The desk page's current screen is the box
around every monitor. With more than one monitor lit, that box is the
wrong size and shape for a page's `screen`: a video player sizing
fullscreen video to it draws the video wider than the window and crops
its sides.

- RenderWidgetHostViewChildFrame narrows the current screen to the
  monitor its view overlaps most, upright or on its side as that monitor
  is.
- Its id and scale stay the desk's: the frame is drawn in the desk's
  window.
- Outside a desk the parent's screens are unchanged.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on crux.
---
 .../renderer_host/render_widget_host_view_child_frame.cc  | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_view_child_frame.cc b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_view_child_frame.cc
index 1adc151..49dd25c 100644
--- a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_view_child_frame.cc
+++ b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_view_child_frame.cc
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 #include "components/viz/common/surfaces/parent_local_surface_id_allocator.h"
 #include "components/viz/host/host_frame_sink_manager.h"
 #include "content/browser/compositor/surface_utils.h"
+#include "content/browser/domicile/domicile_desk.h"
 #include "content/browser/gpu/compositor_util.h"
 #include "content/browser/renderer_host/cross_process_frame_connector.h"
 #include "content/browser/renderer_host/frame_connector.h"
@@ -581,8 +582,13 @@ void RenderWidgetHostViewChildFrame::UpdateCursor(const ui::Cursor& cursor) {
 }
 
 void RenderWidgetHostViewChildFrame::UpdateScreenInfo() {
+  // DOMICILE: a frame inherits its parent's screens, and a desk page's
+  // current screen is the whole desk. A frame gets the monitor it is on, as
+  // a browser window does, so a fullscreen video fits that monitor. See
+  // content/browser/domicile/domicile_desk.h.
   if (frame_connector_)
-    screen_infos_ = frame_connector_->GetScreenInfos();
+    screen_infos_ = DomicileFrameScreenInfos(frame_connector_->GetScreenInfos(),
+                                             GetViewBounds());
 }
 
 void RenderWidgetHostViewChildFrame::SendInitialPropertiesIfNeeded() {
